# requirements/data-sources/local.ears
capability: Local folder sources (a person's own frames)
owner: data-sources
requirements:
  - id: LOC-001
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The system shall open a local source's files for reading only, and write everything it derives from them under SDP's data folder, which never lies inside a source."
    rationale: "The frames are the person's originals (575 GB on D:\\astrophotography); a tool that could write there could lose them (#71)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.local.test_local_index::test_nothing_is_ever_written_under_the_source"
      - "python/tests.local.test_local_index::test_a_source_and_the_data_folder_never_hold_each_other"
  - id: LOC-002
    pattern: event
    text: "When a local source is indexed, the system shall read each new or changed frame's primary header up to its END card, never its pixels, into one index row per frame."
    rationale: "21,000 frames of 25 MB each are read in minutes when only their header blocks are read; a rerun reads only what changed (#71)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.local.test_local_index::test_only_the_header_is_read_never_the_pixels"
      - "python/tests.local.test_local_index::test_the_index_has_one_row_per_frame_with_its_kind_and_exposure"
      - "python/tests.local.test_local_index::test_a_rerun_reads_only_new_or_changed_files"
      - "python/tests.local.test_local_index::test_the_commands_add_index_and_report_with_no_database"
  - id: LOC-003
    pattern: event
    text: "When SDP plate-solves a local frame, the system shall accept the solution only with at least the configured number of Gaia stars matched and a fit RMS under the configured limit, and otherwise record the frame as unsolved with the reason."
    rationale: "A doubtful sky solution would put every later measurement in the wrong place; a refusal with its reason can be fixed or retried (#71). Defaults: 12 stars, 1.5 arcsec."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.local.test_plate_solver::test_a_rotated_bayer_frame_far_from_its_object_solves_to_half_an_arcsecond"
      - "python/tests.local.test_plate_solver::test_any_rotation_and_a_mirrored_frame_solve"
      - "python/tests.local.test_plate_solver::test_a_stacked_colour_master_solves_from_its_luminance"
      - "python/tests.local.test_plate_solver::test_a_frame_with_too_few_stars_is_refused_with_its_reason"
      - "python/tests.local.test_plate_solver::test_a_wrong_scale_is_refused_not_forced"
      - "python/tests.local.test_plate_solver::test_an_rms_over_the_limit_is_refused"
  - id: LOC-004
    pattern: event
    text: "When a batch of local frames is solved, the system shall write each solution or refusal under the data folder's solutions directory at the frame's relative path, and skip on a later run every frame already solved or refused unless asked to redo it."
    rationale: "7,745 M31 frames are solved in batches over several sittings; a rerun continues where the last one stopped, reading one Gaia cone per target (#71)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.local.test_plate_solver::test_a_batch_writes_solutions_and_refusals_under_the_data_folder_only"
      - "python/tests.local.test_plate_solver::test_the_command_solves_against_gaia_through_the_acquisition_cache"
  - id: LOC-005
    pattern: event
    text: "When an investigation profile names an indexed local source as an observation archive, the system shall offer as images only that source's dated, solved light and stack frames that reach the field, each read in place and given its sky solution in the image header."
    rationale: "The person's own frames answer the same question as an archive's images (is each Gaia star where its motion puts it?); a frame with no solution or date cannot be compared with Gaia, and the source folder is never written to (#71)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3, T4]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.local.test_local_gateway::test_a_search_lists_the_dated_solved_frames_that_reach_the_target"
      - "python/tests.local.test_local_gateway::test_an_unsolved_or_calibration_frame_is_never_offered"
      - "python/tests.local.test_local_gateway::test_a_cutout_carries_the_frames_solution_onto_its_own_pixels"
      - "python/tests.local.test_local_gateway::test_a_cutout_off_the_frame_is_refused"
      - "python/tests.local.test_local_gateway::test_the_dialect_curates_a_whole_solved_frame_and_leaves_the_rest"
      - "python/tests.local.test_local_gateway::test_bootstrap_offers_each_indexed_local_source"
      - "python/tests.local.test_local_gateway::test_the_my_frames_profile_finds_the_one_gaia_star_the_frames_do_not_show"
      - "python/tests.local.test_sidecars::test_a_binned_image_keeps_the_frames_distortion"
  - id: LOC-006
    pattern: event
    text: "When a local frame has no solved frame in its folder and no OBJECT name with a known position, the system shall start its solution from the header's RA and DEC pointing, rounded to 0.1 degree."
    rationale: "Some frames carry a UUID where the target's name belongs but still say where the telescope pointed; rounding lets the frames of one target share one Gaia read (#71)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.local.test_offline_solving::test_the_headers_pointing_is_read_as_degrees_or_sexagesimal"
      - "python/tests.local.test_offline_solving::test_an_index_from_before_the_pointing_columns_is_read_again"
      - "python/tests.local.test_offline_solving::test_a_frame_with_no_usable_name_solves_from_its_headers_pointing"
  - id: LOC-007
    pattern: event
    text: "When a local frame's OBJECT name is not in the source's names file, the system shall ask SIMBAD for it at most once per run and keep the answer in the names file, never replacing a position the person gave."
    rationale: "Gaia is local (216 GB), so the names of a few dozen targets were the only reason solving needed the network; once they are in the file, solving runs offline (#71)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.local.test_offline_solving::test_each_name_is_asked_of_simbad_once_and_later_runs_need_no_network"
      - "python/tests.local.test_offline_solving::test_an_unreachable_simbad_refuses_with_how_to_give_the_centre"
      - "python/tests.local.test_offline_solving::test_a_centre_you_give_is_kept_and_simbad_never_overwrites_it"
      - "python/tests.local.test_offline_solving::test_the_names_command_keeps_centres_you_give"
  - id: LOC-008
    pattern: event
    text: "When a frame in the same folder is already solved, the system shall start from the nearest such frame's solution and use the triangle search only if that start fails the limits of LOC-003."
    rationale: "Subs a few seconds apart differ by a small turn of the field; starting from the last one skips the triangle search, and the same limits keep a wrong start from being accepted (#71)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.local.test_offline_solving::test_a_neighbours_solution_refines_to_the_frame_or_is_refused"
      - "python/tests.local.test_offline_solving::test_a_folder_chains_each_frame_from_its_solved_neighbour_and_falls_back_to_triangles"
  - id: LOC-009
    pattern: event
    text: "When local frames are solved by several workers, the system shall solve or refuse the same frames as one worker would."
    rationale: "20,773 frames are solved overnight on several cores; the number of workers changes the time taken, not the results (#71)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.local.test_offline_solving::test_several_workers_solve_the_same_frames_as_one"
  - id: LOC-010
    pattern: event
    text: "When a local frame is solved or refused after being read, the system shall record the SHA-256 of the bytes it read with the result."
    rationale: "Solving reads every pixel anyway, so the fingerprint that later shows the original is intact costs no extra pass over 575 GB (#71)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.local.test_offline_solving::test_a_solution_records_the_fingerprint_of_the_bytes_it_read"
  - id: LOC-011
    pattern: event
    text: "When a local source is verified, the system shall report each frame that is missing, new, modified or corrupted against its first recorded SHA-256 and keep that fingerprint unless asked to accept the change."
    rationale: "Size and date catch edits but not bits gone bad on a drive; a fingerprint that followed every change could never show one (#71)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.local.test_offline_solving::test_verify_finds_missing_modified_and_corrupted_frames_and_keeps_the_first_fingerprints"
      - "python/tests.local.test_offline_solving::test_the_verify_and_manifest_commands"
  - id: LOC-012
    pattern: event
    text: "When a local frame is solved, the system shall write its solution beside the solution file as a header-only FITS .wcs file that gives the same sky positions as SDP's own solution."
    rationale: "Siril, ASTAP, DS9 and astropy read FITS WCS headers, not SDP's JSON; the frame itself is never written to, so the header travels beside it (#71)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.local.test_sidecars::test_each_solution_has_a_wcs_file_that_astropy_reads_as_sdp_does"
      - "python/tests.local.test_sidecars::test_the_sidecars_command_writes_missing_wcs_files_and_a_refusal_removes_one"
  - id: LOC-013
    pattern: event
    text: "When a solved local frame has at least the configured number of matched stars, the system shall add a SIP distortion polynomial only if it lowers the RMS on held-out stars below nine tenths of a TAN fit's."
    rationale: "A 1.6 degree field bends by an arcsecond or more at its corners; holding every fourth star out of the fit keeps noise from being taken for distortion (#71). Defaults: 40 stars, order 2 or 3."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.local.test_sidecars::test_a_bent_field_gets_a_distortion_polynomial_that_follows_it"
      - "python/tests.local.test_sidecars::test_a_straight_field_keeps_its_plain_tan_solution"
      - "python/tests.local.test_sidecars::test_a_frame_with_few_stars_is_not_given_a_polynomial"
  - id: LOC-014
    pattern: event
    text: "When solved local frames are exported, the system shall write each copy outside the source with the solution in its header and the original's pixel bytes unchanged, skipping any frame whose bytes differ from the ones solved."
    rationale: "Some software reads only a frame's own header; a copy must never change the data or describe a file other than the one solved, and the original is never written to (#71)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.local.test_sidecars::test_a_solved_copy_has_the_wcs_in_its_header_and_the_original_pixel_bytes"
      - "python/tests.local.test_sidecars::test_an_export_into_the_source_or_of_changed_bytes_is_refused"
  - id: LOC-015
    pattern: event
    text: "When a local frame is solved, the system shall record with its solution the frame's star width, ellipticity, sky background and gradient, zero point against Gaia G, limiting magnitude, star counts and trails, measured from the solving pass."
    rationale: "Clouds, wind, dew, moonlight and satellites spoil frames without stopping them solving; measuring them from the stars already found costs no extra read of the file (#71)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.local.test_quality::test_a_solved_frame_records_its_sharpness_sky_transparency_and_depth"
      - "python/tests.local.test_quality::test_cloud_wind_and_a_satellite_show_in_the_measures"
  - id: LOC-016
    pattern: event
    text: "When a local source is graded, the system shall grade each solved frame good, usable or poor against the other frames of its session with the reasons in words, and grade a refused frame poor with its refusal."
    rationale: "A 10 s sub and a three-hour stack share no fixed limits, so a frame is judged against its own night's frames; fewer than five frames are not compared (#71)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.local.test_quality::test_a_frame_is_graded_against_its_own_session_with_its_reasons"
      - "python/tests.local.test_quality::test_a_small_session_is_not_compared"
      - "python/tests.local.test_quality::test_the_quality_command_grades_every_session_and_summarises_each_night"
  - id: LOC-017
    pattern: event
    text: "When a graded local source is offered as an observation archive, the system shall leave out its frames graded poor unless asked to include them."
    rationale: "A blurred or cloudy frame would flag Gaia stars it simply failed to show; leaving it out keeps a flag a lead rather than noise (#71)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.local.test_quality::test_the_image_gateway_leaves_out_poor_frames"
  - id: LOC-018
    pattern: event
    text: "When a local source's catalogue is built, the system shall write one row per indexed frame with its status, night, exposure and grade, and for a solved frame its centre, corners, radius and solution quality."
    rationale: "One table answers what was taken, where, when and how well, for SDP and for any tool that reads Parquet; it is rebuilt from the index, solutions and grades, so it never disagrees with them (#71)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.local.test_catalogue::test_the_catalogue_has_every_frame_with_its_footprint_status_and_night"
  - id: LOC-019
    pattern: event
    text: "When local frames are searched for a place on the sky, the system shall list the solved frames whose four-cornered footprint reaches within the given radius of it, filtered by kind, grade and night."
    rationale: "Which frames cover this spot, and when, is the first question of any follow-up; testing the footprint rather than a circle about the centre keeps a star near a corner from being missed or wrongly offered (#71)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.local.test_catalogue::test_find_lists_the_solved_frames_over_a_place_by_kind_grade_and_night"
      - "python/tests.local.test_catalogue::test_the_find_and_coverage_commands"
  - id: LOC-020
    pattern: event
    text: "When the planner matches a requirement, the system shall describe each indexed local source from its catalogue as an image archive covering its sessions' cones and dates."
    rationale: "sdp plan could not see the person's frames because no descriptor named them; described from the catalogue, the frames are planned and costed like any archive's images (#71)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3, T4]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.local.test_catalogue::test_the_solved_frames_are_described_like_any_archive"
      - "python/tests.local.test_catalogue::test_the_planner_plans_cutouts_of_the_frames_over_a_field"
  - id: LOC-021
    pattern: event
    text: "When light curves are built for a local target, the system shall measure each Gaia star on the target's solved subs at its proper-motion position and calibrate every frame against comparison stars of the field."
    rationale: "Leigh's subs span many nights of the same targets; placing each star from the frame's own solution and fitting each frame's zero point and colour term on steady comparison stars turns those subs into light curves on Gaia's G scale, with haze and airmass taken out (#71)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.local.test_lightcurves::test_each_star_gets_a_calibrated_curve_and_the_variable_stands_out"
      - "python/tests.local.test_lightcurves::test_the_curves_and_the_nightly_means_are_written_beside_the_summary"
      - "python/tests.local.test_lightcurves::test_the_target_with_the_most_nights_and_its_cone_are_the_defaults"
      - "python/tests.local.test_lightcurves::test_the_lightcurve_command"
  - id: LOC-022
    pattern: event
    text: "When an investigation asks a local source for light curves, the system shall offer each measured star's curve as a canonical light-curve product within the match radius of the star."
    rationale: "Offered as products, the person's own curves go through the same variability test as WISE's and DASCH's, so a star is flagged against its neighbours' scatter with the run recorded like any other (#71)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3, T4]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.local.test_lightcurves::test_the_gateway_offers_each_measured_star_as_a_light_curve"
      - "python/tests.local.test_lightcurves::test_the_variability_profile_flags_only_the_variable"
